{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2752 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "2d5db09f6ff9649a6d90b7704cc273b20cc955b4c6d57ac75c5745f013078f32" :edb/db-before-t 2751 :edb/db-after-t 2752 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536064 50 #inst "2026-10-09T14:08:03.134Z" 13194139536064 true] [17592186152210 1020 #edb/ref 17592186381848 13194139536064 true] [17592186152211 1020 #edb/ref 17592186381834 13194139536064 true] [17592186152212 1020 #edb/ref 17592186381841 13194139536064 true] [17592186152212 1020 #edb/ref 17592186381855 13194139536064 true] [17592186152560 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536064 true] [17592186152560 1100 "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+16y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=A\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+B\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x,\n$$\n\nsolve the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+16y=0,\\,y(0)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-4.\n$$" 13194139536064 true] [17592186152560 1100 "Given that the differential equation\n\n$y^{″} + 16y = 0$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$y = A\\sin 4x + B\\cos 4x$,\n\nsolve the following initial value problem:\n\n$y^{″} + 16y = 0, y(0) = 1, y^{′}(0) =-4$." 13194139536064 false] [17592186152560 1145 "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=-4,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=4A\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x-4B\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=-4$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4=4A\\,⟹\\,A=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x.\n$$" 13194139536064 true] [17592186381834 1017 #edb/ref 17592186381835 13194139536064 true] [17592186381834 1089 "q-130353" 13194139536064 true] [17592186381834 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536064 true] [17592186381834 1100 "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+81y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=A\\operatorname{sin}⁡9x+B\\operatorname{cos}⁡9x,\n$$\n\nsolve the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+81y=0,\\,y(0)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-9.\n$$" 13194139536064 true] [17592186381834 1113 #uuid "5484a5c3-0023-5cdb-b78a-d2038bca8aa0" 13194139536064 true] [17592186381834 1145 "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=-9,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=9A\\operatorname{cos}⁡9x-9B\\operatorname{sin}⁡9x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=-9$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9=9A\\,⟹\\,A=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡9x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡9x.\n$$" 13194139536064 true] [17592186381835 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381836 13194139536064 true] [17592186381835 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381837 13194139536064 true] [17592186381835 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381838 13194139536064 true] [17592186381835 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381839 13194139536064 true] [17592186381835 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381840 13194139536064 true] [17592186381835 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536064 true] [17592186381835 1041 "selection" 13194139536064 true] [17592186381835 1104 #edb/ref 17592186381837 13194139536064 true] [17592186381835 1110 #uuid "267b02e2-9111-5156-8c9e-c0a81bc71524" 13194139536064 true] [17592186381836 1034 "y=9\\operatorname{sin}⁡9x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡9x" 13194139536064 true] [17592186381836 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536064 true] [17592186381836 1111 #uuid "3461801c-a6fc-502a-aada-47a46b1e5abb" 13194139536064 true] [17592186381837 1034 "y=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡9x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡9x" 13194139536064 true] [17592186381837 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536064 true] [17592186381837 1111 #uuid "d5a1bee4-8e74-5567-a724-4c5b712d6017" 13194139536064 true] [17592186381838 1034 "y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡9x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡9x" 13194139536064 true] [17592186381838 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536064 true] [17592186381838 1111 #uuid "fa8bf968-74ab-505f-aeb8-f8fa66640eb9" 13194139536064 true] [17592186381839 1034 "y=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡9x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡9x" 13194139536064 true] [17592186381839 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536064 true] [17592186381839 1111 #uuid "8ea08fb9-6a13-50a6-8169-a1f5974c0ae4" 13194139536064 true] [17592186381840 1034 "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡9x" 13194139536064 true] [17592186381840 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536064 true] [17592186381840 1111 #uuid "67e15767-19e6-5657-8520-f74c4f5015ba" 13194139536064 true] [17592186381841 1017 #edb/ref 17592186381842 13194139536064 true] [17592186381841 1089 "q-130374" 13194139536064 true] [17592186381841 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536064 true] [17592186381841 1100 "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+2y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x),\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+2y=0,\\,y(0)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-2.\n$$" 13194139536064 true] [17592186381841 1113 #uuid "1e41e4a4-a4ff-518a-ba3d-1adb97965117" 13194139536064 true] [17592186381841 1145 "We find the constants $P$ and $Q$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nP=2.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=-2,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-{e}^{-x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+{e}^{-x}(-P\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+Q\\operatorname{cos}⁡x).\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(0)=-2$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n-P+Q=-2.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $P=2$ gives $Q=0.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536064 true] [17592186381842 1000 #edb/ref 1759218638184